# An Adventure's "instead of putting [it] into its owner's graveyard as it resolves, its controller exiles it" (CR 715.3d) is a
# replacement effect (CR 614.1a), ordered by the spell's controller with the others that would change the move (CR 616.1).
# Bot2's Dauthi Voidwalker ("If a card would be put into an opponent's graveyard from anywhere, instead exile it with a void
# counter on it") is out by turn 3, when Bot1 casts Bonecrusher Giant as Stomp at Bot2. As Stomp resolves Bot1 takes the
# Voidwalker's first: the card is exiled with a void counter, the Adventure's exile no longer applies (CR 616.1f), and the
# card is not on an Adventure - Bot1 is never offered the Giant from exile. On turn 6 Bot2 sacrifices the Voidwalker and casts
# the Giant, the one void-countered card, for free.

